{"resource": {"name": "Bacteria Sample Data", "id": "e49x-tw9b", "resource_name": null, "parent_fxf": [], "description": "Samples are taken daily at locations throughout the distribution system. Temperature, pH, and Total Chlorine Residual are collected by city personnel. Samples are taken to a lab to be analyzed for Total Coliform and E. Coli indicators. Results are returned to the city the following business day.", "attribution": null, "attribution_link": null, "contact_email": null, "type": "dataset", "updatedAt": "2025-01-28T11:31:30.000Z", "createdAt": "2018-10-31T19:18:11.000Z", "metadata_updated_at": "2025-01-28T11:31:24.000Z", "data_updated_at": "2025-01-28T11:31:30.000Z", "columns_name": ["Sample Type", "Free Chlorine", "Street", "Total Chlorine Residual", "DATE", "Replacement Address/Notes", "SITE #", "RESULTS", "Number of Samples Taken"], "columns_field_name": ["replacement_sample", "free_chlorine", "street", "total_chlorine_residual", "date", "replacement_address_or_notes", "site", "results", "number_of_samples_taken"], "columns_datatype": ["Text", "Number", "Text", "Number", "Calendar date", "Text", "Text", "Text", "Number"], "columns_description": ["Bacteria Samples are routine and collected every 30 days. If a sample has an error, is rejected, or has bacteria present, a replacement sample is taken. This column indicates if the sample is a replacement. Special Samples are locations that are not normally sampled. Refer to the notes section to determine why sample was taken.", "The amount of free chlorine as measured in mg/L. This number increases in Feb/Mar during the chlorine maintenance period. Instruments have an accuracy of plus or minus 0.1 mg/L.", "Street name for where water sample was collected.", "The level of chlorine disinfectant by measuring chloramines (minimum requirement is .5 mg/L). Instruments have an accuracy of plus or minus 0.1 mg/L.", "Date test was conducted.", "Indicates the location of replacement samples, special samples, or any